#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:1
msgid "12. LLM Inference on DGX Spark"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:3
msgid ""
"DGX Spark's unified memory can hold Qwen3-32B in 16-bit precision. We'll run "
"it with [Grout](https://github.com/huggingface/grout), an inference engine "
"built on cuTile Rust, starting with the smaller Qwen3-4B model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:7
msgid ""
"The measurements below are from a DGX Spark (GB10, `sm_121`, 20 CPU cores, "
"128 GB of unified LPDDR5X memory) running DGX OS with the 580 driver and "
"CUDA 13.4. They use cuTile Rust 0.4.0 (tag `cutile-rs/v0.4.0` in the [cuda-"
"rust repository](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust)) and Grout at commit "
"[`deb7427`](https://github.com/elibol/grout/commit/"
"deb74274c731d4ca9e7f9b356a91892398498309)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:15
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:17
msgid ""
"The DGX OS image used here ships CUDA 13.0, which is too old for cuTile and "
"lacks the Tile IR assembler. Install a current toolkit alongside 13.0:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:20
msgid ""
"sudo apt-get install -y cuda-toolkit-13-4 cuda-tileiras-13-4\n"
"sudo apt-get install -y clang libclang-dev cmake build-essential pkg-config\n"
"curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y --"
"default-toolchain nightly\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:26
msgid "Then point the toolchain at the new toolkit (add these to `~/.bashrc`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:28
msgid ""
"export CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-13.4\n"
"export CUDA_TOOLKIT_PATH=$CUDA_HOME\n"
"export PATH=$CUDA_HOME/bin:$HOME/.cargo/bin:$PATH\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:34
msgid ""
"`CUDA_TOOLKIT_PATH` takes precedence over `CUDA_HOME`. Setting it also "
"overrides the `/usr/local/cuda-13` default in Grout's `.cargo/config.toml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:37
msgid "Check that both CUDA tools report release 13.4 and Cargo uses nightly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:39
msgid ""
"nvcc --version\n"
"tileiras --version\n"
"cargo --version\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:45
msgid ""
"The 580 driver is a CUDA 13.0 driver. CUDA's minor-version compatibility "
"lets 13.x toolkits run on it, and the Tile IR assembler emits native "
"`sm_121` code rather than PTX, so nothing in this tutorial needs a newer "
"driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:51
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:53
msgid ""
"These commands keep the model directories and cuTile Rust checkout next to "
"Grout:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:55
msgid ""
"~/dev/\n"
"  cuda-rust/     # CUDA Rust checkout at tag cutile-rs/v0.4.0\n"
"  cutile-rs/     # symlink to cuda-rust/cutile-rs (Grout builds against it)\n"
"  grout/         # the inference engine\n"
"  hf_models/\n"
"    qwen3_4b/\n"
"    qwen3_32b/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:65
msgid ""
"mkdir -p ~/dev && cd ~/dev\n"
"git clone --branch cutile-rs/v0.4.0 https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust.git\n"
"ln -s cuda-rust/cutile-rs cutile-rs\n"
"git clone https://github.com/elibol/grout.git\n"
"git -C grout checkout deb74274c731d4ca9e7f9b356a91892398498309\n"
"pip install -U \"huggingface_hub[cli]\"\n"
"hf download Qwen/Qwen3-4B  --local-dir hf_models/qwen3_4b    # about 8 GB\n"
"hf download Qwen/Qwen3-32B --local-dir hf_models/qwen3_32b   # about 66 GB\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:76
msgid ""
"Grout's pinned commit depends on cuTile Rust 0.4.0. Its `[patch.crates-io]` "
"uses the sibling `cutile-rs` path, which the symlink above resolves into the "
"CUDA Rust checkout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:80
msgid ""
"Build Grout in release mode. On the Spark this takes well under a minute "
"after the dependencies are compiled once:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:83
msgid "cd ~/dev/grout && cargo build --release\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:87
msgid ""
"This builds the inference binary. The autotuner requires the `benchmarks` "
"feature; see [Autotuning](#autotuning) below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:92
msgid "First run: Qwen3-4B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:94
msgid ""
"cargo run --release -- \\\n"
"  --model ../hf_models/qwen3_4b \\\n"
"  --prompt \"Explain unified memory on DGX Spark in three sentences.\" \\\n"
"  --max-new-tokens 200 --profile\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:101
msgid ""
"These runs use Grout's built-in tuning defaults. The pinned revision ships "
"records for `sm_100` and `sm_120`; with no `benchmarks/tuning/sm_121/` "
"directory, Grout uses the defaults without printing a warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:105
msgid ""
"On the first run, cuTile compiles Grout's kernels from Rust through Tile IR "
"to `sm_121` machine code and caches them on disk. Later runs load the "
"compiled kernels from the cache."
msgstr ""

