msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:118
msgid ""
"`--profile` prints prefill and decode step averages. `GROUT_PROFILE_OPS=1` "
"adds a per-operation table; `GROUT_PROFILE_SYNC_OPS=1` synchronizes after "
"each operation to include GPU execution time. The table covers prefill and "
"warm-up. Decode replays a CUDA graph, so its operations are not timed "
"individually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:123
msgid ""
"GROUT_PROFILE_OPS=1 GROUT_PROFILE_SYNC_OPS=1 cargo run --release -- \\\n"
"  --model ../hf_models/qwen3_4b \\\n"
"  --prompt \"Explain unified memory on DGX Spark in three sentences.\" \\\n"
"  --max-new-tokens 200 --profile\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:130
msgid ""
"Use these settings to inspect individual operations, then unset them when "
"measuring throughput: synchronization changes execution timing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:136
msgid "Qwen3-32B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:138
msgid ""
"Qwen3-32B has 32.8 billion parameters, about 66 GB in 16-bit precision, plus "
"a KV cache that grows with context length (roughly 9 GB at 32K tokens). Both "
"fit in the Spark's 128 GB of unified memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:142
msgid ""
"cargo run --release -- \\\n"
"  --model ../hf_models/qwen3_32b \\\n"
"  --prompt \"What is 2 + 2? Then explain why in one paragraph.\" \\\n"
"  --max-new-tokens 64 --max-seq-len 4096 --profile\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "Qwen3-32B, 16-bit weights"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "Measured"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "3.7 tokens/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "Weights in memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "66 GB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:154
msgid ""
"Both models use the same 37 compiled kernels. Qwen3-32B reads more weight "
"data for each generated token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:159
msgid "Where the time goes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:161
msgid ""
"Decoding one token requires reading every weight once. At 66 GB per token, "
"3.7 tokens per second is about 245 GB/s of sustained memory traffic; the "
"Spark's LPDDR5X peaks near 273 GB/s. For the 4B model, 8 GB per token at "
"29.5 tokens per second is about 236 GB/s. In both cases decode runs at "
"roughly 90% of the memory roofline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:166
msgid ""
"`GROUT_ATTN_BN_DECODE` sets Grout's decode attention tile size (default 32). "
"The following runs varied it manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "`GROUT_ATTN_BN_DECODE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "Qwen3-4B decode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "29.1 tokens/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "32"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:0
msgid "28.9 tokens/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:175
msgid ""
"Changing the tile size has little effect on decode: each token still "
"requires the same weight data. **Prefill** is compute-bound and responds to "
"tile shapes. Use a long prompt (thousands of tokens) and the per-kernel "
"profiler to measure the effect of tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:180
msgid ""
"**Lower-precision weights** halve or quarter the bytes per token with 8-bit "
"or 4-bit formats. The [NVFP4 tutorial](./11-nvfp4-inference.md) covers the "
"kernels for 4-bit inference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:184
msgid ""
"Different tile sizes change the order of floating-point accumulation, which "
"can change the token selected by greedy decoding when logits are nearly "
"tied. The 16 and 64 runs produced the same text as each other, but diverged "
"from the default after the second sentence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:189
msgid "Autotuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:191
msgid "Build the autotuner from the Grout checkout:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:193
msgid ""
"cargo build --release --features benchmarks --bin grout_autotune\n"
"target/release/grout_autotune --help\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:198
msgid ""
"For a prefill attention sweep, use `--site prefill_attention` and a `--"
"prompt-dir` containing `pp_512.txt`, `pp_2048.txt`, and `pp_8192.txt`. "
"Grout's `benchmarks/make_prompts.py` generates these files using the model's "
"tokenizer; it requires the Python `transformers` package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:203
msgid ""
"The tuner writes records and trial logs under `benchmarks/tuning/sm_121/` by "
"default. `--budget-min` limits search time per prompt-length bucket. "
"Rerunning the same command resumes from the trial logs. If allocation "
"recovery exits with code 3, rerun it in a fresh process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:208
msgid ""
"The measurements above use built-in defaults. Generate records on the Spark "
"and compare timings with the defaults before adopting them. Keep the "
"`sm_120` records in their own directory; those were tuned on an RTX 5090."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:215
msgid "Unified memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:217
msgid ""
"The Spark's CPU and GPU share physical memory through a coherent address "
"space (ATS mode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:220
msgid ""
"**Host memory is device memory.** A pageable host buffer's address is valid "
"on the GPU: wrapping a `Vec` with `Tensor::from_foreign` and launching a "
"kernel on it works. The driver's pointer-attribute query does not classify "
"such pointers, so code that validates device pointers that way needs another "
"check on this platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/12-dgx-spark-inference.md:224
msgid ""
"**Readback into fresh pageable memory is slow.** Copying a 256 MB tensor to "
"a newly allocated host `Vec` ran at 0.13 GB/s, against 18.6 GB/s for the "
"host-to-device direction and 24 GB/s for a host `memcpy`. The page faults on "
"the destination dominate. Reuse or pre-touch destination buffers, or use "
"pinned host memory, when readback is on a hot path."
msgstr ""

